      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is not uncommon for residents to experience subtle discomfort from the combination of HVAC operation and smart building automation in dense developments like Hudson Yards, even if the source sounds sub-audible. While low-frequency noise can sometimes influence mood through physiological pathways like resonance, it is highly unlikely that a building system is intentionally designed to emit harmful patterns specifically intended to induce anxiety. I strongly recommend consulting your building management or a professional acoustics consultant to perform a source identification audit, as this can often rule out mechanical faults or settle these feelings of unease by addressing the actual cause.",
